<h2>The Ten Commandments of CLAUDE.md &mdash; Ten Promises for Taming Your AI Pair Programmer</h2>

<p>Anyone who has had an AI write code has lived through it &mdash; the moment it builds a feature nobody asked for, &ldquo;improves&rdquo; perfectly healthy code next door, and shouts &ldquo;All done!&rdquo; without ever running the tests. <strong>CLAUDE.md is the project instruction file that prevents those accidents.</strong> Claude Code reads it automatically at the start of every conversation, so think of it as <strong>the onboarding document you leave on your AI new hire's desk</strong>. This document introduces one especially well-organized set of them &mdash; the <strong>&lsquo;Ten Commandments&rsquo; CLAUDE.md</strong> &mdash; as an infographic, the English original, and a full translation, and covers how best to put it to work.</p>

